    "notes": "Open score, one staff per part, every staff labelled (full names on page 1, then S./A./T./B.). MUST NOT create extra parts for the divisi passages: in mm.7-8 the Tenor staff splits into two voices (\"div.\", stems up/down, back to \"unis.\" in m.9) - both voices belong to the Tenor part (truth: Tenor voice 1 and voice 2); in m.18 and mm.20-21 the Soprano sings two-note chords on one stem and in mm.20-21 the Bass sings octave chords: these stay chords inside Soprano/Bass. Exactly 4 parts. The tenor clef is a treble clef with a small 8 below (sounds an octave lower than written): truth pitches are sounding pitches (e.g. m.16 tenor B3 natural). Lyrics are printed under every staff and belong to each part (the second tenor voice in mm.7-8 has none)."
